468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 159 0 R
/T (Most behavioural variables \(Hours Studied, Attendance, Sleep Hours, Previous Scores\) are approximately symmetric \(skewness close to 0\), so their mean and median are very close and either is a representative measure of centre. Tutoring Sessions is more right-skewed \(skew = 0.82\), reflecting that most students attend few tutoring sessions while a minority attend many; for this variable the median \(1 session\) is a more representative 'typical' value than the mean, which is pulled upward by the small number of high- tutoring students. Exam Score is mildly right-skewed after cleaning \(skew = 1.64\), again meaning the median is a slightly more robust summary of typical performance than the mean, although the two remain close in practice.)
/E (Most behavioural variables \(Hours Studied, Attendance, Sleep Hours, Previous Scores\) are approximately symmetric \(skewness close to 0\), so their mean and median are very close and either is a representative measure of centre. Tutoring Sessions is more right-skewed \(skew = 0.82\), reflecting that most students attend few tutoring sessions while a minority attend many; for this variable the median \(1 session\) is a more representative 'typical' value than the mean, which is pulled upward by the small number of high- tutoring students. Exam Score is mildly right-skewed after cleaning \(skew = 1.64\), again meaning the median is a slightly more robust summary of typical performance than the mean, although the two remain close in practice.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
