/T (It is important to note that the correlations reported in Section 6.2 \(e.g. Attendance and Hours Studied with Exam Score\) describe association, not causation. Students who attend more and study more may also differ in other unmeasured ways \(such as motivation or family support\) that independently affect performance; the regression model in Sections 9-10 quantifies predictive association, not a causal effect of any single variable.)
/E (It is important to note that the correlations reported in Section 6.2 \(e.g. Attendance and Hours Studied with Exam Score\) describe association, not causation. Students who attend more and study more may also differ in other unmeasured ways \(such as motivation or family support\) that independently affect performance; the regression model in Sections 9-10 quantifies predictive association, not a causal effect of any single variable.)
