/E (Comparing train and test performance: Linear Regression's R-squared changed only marginally between train \(0.7175\) and test \(0.7701\), indicating a well-fitted model with no meaningful overfitting. The Random Forest model showed a noticeably larger gap between train R-squared \(0.8365\) and test R-squared \(0.65\), a signature of mild overfitting despite the max_depth constraint used to regularise the trees. This further supports selecting Linear Regression as the preferred model for this problem.)
