/Title (X \(features\) consists of the 25 variables listed in Section 5.5: original numeric behavioural measures, ordinal-encoded ordered categories, one-hot encoded nominal categories, and the three engineered features. y \(target\) is Exam_Score. The 80/20 train-test split \(Section 5.4\) was performed before fitting the StandardScaler, so no information from the test set influenced the scaling parameters.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1285 0 R
>>
endobj
1300 0 obj
<<
/Title (Two models were trained and compared. Linear Regression was chosen as an interpretable baseline that directly quantifies each feature's contribution via its coefficient, which is valuable for explaining results to non-technical stakeholders. A Random Forest Regressor was chosen as a non-linear alternative capable of capturing interactions and non-linear effects between features, to test whether flexibility beyond a linear form improves predictive accuracy.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1286 0 R
>>
endobj
